body:
You could store these parameters in variables then re-use them in the `init`, `render` and `getWidgetRenderState` calls.

It would simplify the code (no more repeated code) and make it more readable imho:

```js
const renderState = instantSearchInstance.renderState[this.getIndexId()] || {};

const initOptions = {
    uiState,
    helper: this.getHelper()!,
    parent: this,
    instantSearchInstance,
    state: helper!.state,
    renderState: instantSearchInstance.renderState,
    templatesConfig: instantSearchInstance.templatesConfig,
    createURL,
    results: undefined,
    scopedResults: [],
    searchMetadata: {
        isSearchStalled: instantSearchInstance._isSearchStalled,
    },
};

const widgetRenderState = widget.getWidgetRenderState(renderState, initOptions);
```

